{"title":"Follow the Money — World's Top 100 Wealth Holders","updated":"2026-07-20","baselineDate":"2026-03-01","methodology":"The initial ranking is the Forbes 2026 annual snapshot using market prices and exchange rates from 1 March 2026. It is a baseline, not a claim of current exact wealth. Future refreshes must preserve historical estimates and label the source date.","disclaimer":"Private wealth cannot be measured with complete precision. Net worth is not the same as cash, salary or realised income. A business, trust, foundation, jurisdiction or political connection does not by itself prove misconduct or coordinated activity.","sources":[{"name":"Forbes World Billionaires 2026 — Top 200","type":"Annual wealth estimate","checked":"2026-07-20","url":"https://www.forbes.com.au/news/billionaires/the-forbes-billionaires-list-top-200/"},{"name":"Forbes Real-Time Billionaires","type":"Live secondary estimate","checked":"2026-07-20","url":"https://www.forbes.com/real-time-billionaires/"},{"name":"SEC EDGAR","type":"Primary corporate filings","url":"https://www.sec.gov/edgar/search/"},{"name":"Company annual reports and stock exchange filings","type":"Primary company evidence","url":"evidence-vault.html"},{"name":"Government procurement, lobbying and political finance records","type":"Public-record enrichment","url":"research-tools.html"}],"defaults":{"publicIncome":"Not reliably disclosed. Net-worth movement is not salary or realised income.","liquidity":"Unknown from public rich-list data; requires filings and asset-by-asset analysis.","evidence":"Estimated annual baseline","confidence":"Estimated","sourceDate":"2026-03-01","lastChecked":"2026-07-20","sourceUrl":"https://www.forbes.com.au/news/billionaires/the-forbes-billionaires-list-top-200/"},"industryProfiles":{"Technology":{"wealthMechanism":"Concentrated founder or early shareholder ownership in scalable technology platforms and infrastructure.","repeatableLesson":"Scalable products and retained ownership can compound far beyond salary, but valuation concentration can reverse sharply."},"Fashion & Retail":{"wealthMechanism":"Large equity stakes in global consumer brands, retail networks and associated property holdings.","repeatableLesson":"Brand, distribution and repeat consumer demand can create durable cash flow; public investors should still test valuation and cyclicality."},"Finance & Investments":{"wealthMechanism":"Ownership of investment firms, exchanges, funds, financial data or long-duration capital allocations.","repeatableLesson":"Capital allocation, fees and long time horizons matter; ordinary investors can copy discipline, not privileged deal access."},"Telecom":{"wealthMechanism":"Control of communications infrastructure and recurring subscriber revenue.","repeatableLesson":"Essential infrastructure and recurring revenue can be powerful, but regulation and debt are material risks."},"Diversified":{"wealthMechanism":"Control or inheritance across several operating businesses, holding companies and asset classes.","repeatableLesson":"Holding several cash-generating assets can reduce dependence on one business after wealth is created."},"Food & Beverage":{"wealthMechanism":"Ownership of branded consumer products, distribution networks and private family businesses.","repeatableLesson":"Everyday demand, brands and distribution can compound over generations, though private ownership is often inaccessible."},"Metals & Mining":{"wealthMechanism":"Equity ownership in scarce-resource extraction, processing and industrial supply chains.","repeatableLesson":"Scarcity can produce exceptional gains, but commodity cycles, geopolitics and capital intensity create severe downside."},"Energy":{"wealthMechanism":"Ownership of energy production, storage, battery, fuel or electricity infrastructure.","repeatableLesson":"Energy security and infrastructure attract capital, but policy, commodity prices and execution can dominate returns."},"Logistics":{"wealthMechanism":"Control o